IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `fraud-nouns`
IMPORT `fraud-dates`
IMPORT `fraud-s15`
IMPORT `fraud-penalty`
IMPORT `fraud-s01-s05`

-- Fraud Act 2006: TESTS FOR SECTIONS 1 TO 5.
--
-- Every expected value was decided by reading the section, and written beside the assertion,
-- before the module was run.  A failing assertion here is a finding, not a typo to correct.
-- Each case below is one alleged act.

§ `Tests for sections 1 to 5`

§§ `Fixtures: gains, losses and aims`

`a permanent gain of money by getting it` MEANS `Intended gain` WITH
    `what the gain is in` IS `money`
    `how it is gained` IS `by getting what one does not have`
    `how long it lasts` IS `permanent`

GIVEN thing IS A `Thing gained or lost`
GIVETH AN `Intended gain`
`a gain in` thing MEANS `Intended gain` WITH
    `what the gain is in` IS thing
    `how it is gained` IS `by getting what one does not have`
    `how long it lasts` IS `permanent`

GIVEN thing IS A `Thing gained or lost`
GIVETH AN `Intended loss`
`a loss in` thing MEANS `Intended loss` WITH
    `what the loss is in` IS thing
    `how it is lost` IS `by parting with what one has`
    `how long it lasts` IS `permanent`

GIVEN g IS A MAYBE `Intended gain`
      l IS A MAYBE `Intended loss`
      r IS A MAYBE `Intended loss`
GIVETH AN `Aim`
`an aim of` g l r MEANS `Aim` WITH
    `a gain for himself or another` IS g
    `loss to another` IS l
    `exposing another to a risk of loss` IS r

`no aim at all` MEANS `an aim of` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING
`an aim to gain money` MEANS `an aim of` (JUST `a permanent gain of money by getting it`) NOTHING NOTHING
`an aim to cause loss of money` MEANS `an aim of` NOTHING (JUST (`a loss in` `money`)) NOTHING
`an aim to risk loss of money` MEANS `an aim of` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (`a loss in` `money`))

§§ `Section 5: gain and loss`

-- Source: s 5(2): "property" means any property whether real or personal (including things in
-- action and other intangible property); money is listed separately.
#ASSERT `section 5(2): the thing is property` `real property`
#ASSERT `section 5(2): the thing is property` `personal property`
#ASSERT `section 5(2): the thing is property` `a thing in action`
#ASSERT `section 5(2): the thing is property` `other intangible property`
#ASSERT NOT `section 5(2): the thing is property` `something that is neither money nor property`
#ASSERT NOT `section 5(2): the thing is property` `money`

-- Source: s 5(2)(a): gain and loss extend only to gain or loss in money or other property.
#ASSERT `section 5(2)(a): gain and loss extend only to money or other property` `money`
#ASSERT `section 5(2)(a): gain and loss extend only to money or other property` `real property`
#ASSERT `section 5(2)(a): gain and loss extend only to money or other property` `a thing in action`
#ASSERT NOT `section 5(2)(a): gain and loss extend only to money or other property` `something that is neither money nor property`

-- Source: s 5(2)(b): temporary or permanent.
#ASSERT `section 5(2)(b): gain and loss include a temporary one and a permanent one` `temporary`
#ASSERT `section 5(2)(b): gain and loss include a temporary one and a permanent one` `permanent`

-- Source: s 5(3): a gain includes a gain by keeping what one has, as well as by getting what one does not have.
#ASSERT `section 5(3): a gain includes a gain by keeping what one has` `by keeping what one has`
#ASSERT `section 5(3): a gain includes a gain by keeping what one has` `by getting what one does not have`

-- Source: s 5(4): a loss includes a loss by not getting what one might get, as well as by parting with what one has.
#ASSERT `section 5(4): a loss includes a loss by not getting what one might get` `by not getting what one might get`
#ASSERT `section 5(4): a loss includes a loss by not getting what one might get` `by parting with what one has`

-- Source: s 5(1)-(4) together.  A temporary gain of money by keeping what one has is a gain (3 of 3 limbs).
#ASSERT `section 5: a gain within the meaning of section 5` (`Intended gain` WITH `what the gain is in` IS `money`, `how it is gained` IS `by keeping what one has`, `how long it lasts` IS `temporary`)
-- A gain of a service or of information is not a gain within s 5(2)(a).
#ASSERT NOT `section 5: a gain within the meaning of section 5` (`a gain in` `something that is neither money nor property`)
-- A loss by not getting what one might get, in a thing in action, is a loss.
#ASSERT `section 5: a loss within the meaning of section 5` (`Intended loss` WITH `what the loss is in` IS `a thing in action`, `how it is lost` IS `by not getting what one might get`, `how long it lasts` IS `temporary`)
#ASSERT NOT `section 5: a loss within the meaning of section 5` (`a loss in` `something that is neither money nor property`)

§§ `The intention common to sections 2(1)(b), 3(b) and 4(1)(c)`

-- (i) a gain for himself or another.
#ASSERT `sections 2(1)(b), 3(b) and 4(1)(c): intends a gain for himself or another, or loss to another, or to expose another to a risk of loss` `an aim to gain money`
-- (ii) loss to another.
#ASSERT `sections 2(1)(b), 3(b) and 4(1)(c): intends a gain for himself or another, or loss to another, or to expose another to a risk of loss` `an aim to cause loss of money`
-- (ii) exposing another to a risk of loss.
#ASSERT `sections 2(1)(b), 3(b) and 4(1)(c): intends a gain for himself or another, or loss to another, or to expose another to a risk of loss` `an aim to risk loss of money`
-- No aim at all: not within (i) or (ii).
#ASSERT NOT `sections 2(1)(b), 3(b) and 4(1)(c): intends a gain for himself or another, or loss to another, or to expose another to a risk of loss` `no aim at all`
-- An aim to gain a non-property advantage is not a gain within s 5.
#ASSERT NOT `sections 2(1)(b), 3(b) and 4(1)(c): intends a gain for himself or another, or loss to another, or to expose another to a risk of loss` (`an aim of` (JUST (`a gain in` `something that is neither money nor property`)) NOTHING NOTHING)
-- A non-property gain does not cancel a property loss aimed at: either limb suffices.
#ASSERT `sections 2(1)(b), 3(b) and 4(1)(c): intends a gain for himself or another, or loss to another, or to expose another to a risk of loss` (`an aim of` (JUST (`a gain in` `something that is neither money nor property`)) (JUST (`a loss in` `money`)) NOTHING)

§§ `Section 2: fraud by false representation`

GIVEN about IS A `What a representation is about`
      form IS A `Form of a representation`
      madeTo IS A `Who or what a representation was made to`
      untrue IS A BOOLEAN
      misleading IS A BOOLEAN
      knows IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Representation`
`a representation of` about form madeTo untrue misleading knows MEANS `Representation` WITH
    `what it is about` IS about
    `its form` IS form
    `who or what it was made to` IS madeTo
    `untrue` IS untrue
    `misleading` IS misleading
    `the person making it knows that it is, or might be, untrue or misleading` IS knows

GIVEN rep IS A `Representation`
      dishonest IS A BOOLEAN
      aim IS AN `Aim`
GIVETH A `False representation case`
`a section 2 case of` rep dishonest aim MEANS `False representation case` WITH
    `the representation` IS rep
    `acts dishonestly in making it` IS dishonest
    `what the person intends by making it` IS aim

`a false statement of fact made to a person` MEANS `a representation of` `a fact` `express` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE

-- The base case: every element of s 2(1) made out.
#ASSERT `section 2(1): a person is in breach of section 2` (`a section 2 case of` `a false statement of fact made to a person` TRUE `an aim to gain money`)
-- s 2(1)(a): not dishonest -> not in breach.
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1): a person is in breach of section 2` (`a section 2 case of` `a false statement of fact made to a person` FALSE `an aim to gain money`)
-- s 2(1)(b): no intention of gain or loss -> not in breach (the Act needs the intention).
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1): a person is in breach of section 2` (`a section 2 case of` `a false statement of fact made to a person` TRUE `no aim at all`)
-- s 2(1)(b)(i): intended gain is in a service -> outside s 5, so not in breach of s 2.
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1): a person is in breach of section 2` (`a section 2 case of` `a false statement of fact made to a person` TRUE (`an aim of` (JUST (`a gain in` `something that is neither money nor property`)) NOTHING NOTHING))
-- s 2(1)(b)(ii): the aim is loss to another.
#ASSERT `section 2(1): a person is in breach of section 2` (`a section 2 case of` `a false statement of fact made to a person` TRUE `an aim to cause loss of money`)
-- s 2(1)(b)(ii): the aim is to expose another to a risk of loss.
#ASSERT `section 2(1): a person is in breach of section 2` (`a section 2 case of` `a false statement of fact made to a person` TRUE `an aim to risk loss of money`)

-- s 2(2)(a): untrue OR misleading.  Untrue only, misleading only, both, neither.
#ASSERT `section 2(2): a representation is false` (`a representation of` `a fact` `express` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `section 2(2): a representation is false` (`a representation of` `a fact` `express` `a person` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `section 2(2): a representation is false` (`a representation of` `a fact` `express` `a person` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(2): a representation is false` (`a representation of` `a fact` `express` `a person` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- s 2(2)(b): the person making it must know that it is, or might be, untrue or misleading.
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(2): a representation is false` (`a representation of` `a fact` `express` `a person` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(2): a representation is false` (`a representation of` `a fact` `express` `a person` FALSE TRUE FALSE)

-- s 2(3): a representation as to fact or law, including state of mind of the person or any other person.
#ASSERT `section 2(3): what a representation is about is within the meaning of "representation"` `a fact`
#ASSERT `section 2(3): what a representation is about is within the meaning of "representation"` `the law`
#ASSERT `section 2(3): what a representation is about is within the meaning of "representation"` `the state of mind of the person making it`
#ASSERT `section 2(3): what a representation is about is within the meaning of "representation"` `the state of mind of any other person`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(3): what a representation is about is within the meaning of "representation"` `something other than fact, law or state of mind`
-- A representation about the law, in an implied form, in a case that is otherwise complete, is still within s 2.
#ASSERT `section 2(1): a person is in breach of section 2` (`a section 2 case of` (`a representation of` `the law` `implied` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE) TRUE `an aim to gain money`)
-- A representation about something other than fact, law or state of mind is outside s 2(3).
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1): a person is in breach of section 2` (`a section 2 case of` (`a representation of` `something other than fact, law or state of mind` `express` `a person` TRUE FALSE TRUE) TRUE `an aim to gain money`)
-- s 2(4): express or implied.
#ASSERT `section 2(4): a representation may be express or implied` `express`
#ASSERT `section 2(4): a representation may be express or implied` `implied`

-- s 2(5): submitted to a system or device counts as made, with or without human intervention.
#ASSERT `section 2(1): a person is in breach of section 2` (`a section 2 case of` (`a representation of` `a fact` `express` `a system or device designed to receive, convey or respond to communications` TRUE FALSE TRUE) TRUE `an aim to gain money`)
#ASSERT `section 2(5): a representation may be regarded as made when submitted to a person or to a system or device` `a system or device designed to receive, convey or respond to communications`
-- Never communicated: not made, so no breach.
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(5): a representation may be regarded as made when submitted to a person or to a system or device` `nobody and nothing: it was not communicated`
#ASSERT NOT `section 2(1): a person is in breach of section 2` (`a section 2 case of` (`a representation of` `a fact` `express` `nobody and nothing: it was not communicated` TRUE FALSE TRUE) TRUE `an aim to gain money`)

§§ `Section 3: fraud by failing to disclose information`

GIVEN fails IS A BOOLEAN
      duty IS A BOOLEAN
      dishonest IS A BOOLEAN
      aim IS AN `Aim`
GIVETH A `Non-disclosure case`
`a section 3 case of` fails duty dishonest aim MEANS `Non-disclosure case` WITH
    `fails to disclose information to another person` IS fails
    `the information is information which he is under a legal duty to disclose` IS duty
    `acts dishonestly in failing to disclose it` IS dishonest
    `what the person intends by failing to disclose it` IS aim

-- The base case: all of s 3(a) and (b).
#ASSERT `section 3: a person is in breach of section 3` (`a section 3 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `an aim to gain money`)
-- s 3(a): no failure to disclose.
#ASSERT NOT `section 3: a person is in breach of section 3` (`a section 3 case of` FALSE TRUE TRUE `an aim to gain money`)
-- s 3(a): no legal duty to disclose.
#ASSERT NOT `section 3: a person is in breach of section 3` (`a section 3 case of` TRUE FALSE TRUE `an aim to gain money`)
-- s 3(a): not dishonest.
#ASSERT NOT `section 3: a person is in breach of section 3` (`a section 3 case of` TRUE TRUE FALSE `an aim to gain money`)
-- s 3(b): no aim.
#ASSERT NOT `section 3: a person is in breach of section 3` (`a section 3 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no aim at all`)
-- s 3(b)(ii): aim to cause loss.
#ASSERT `section 3: a person is in breach of section 3` (`a section 3 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `an aim to cause loss of money`)

§§ `Section 4: fraud by abuse of position`

GIVEN occupies IS A BOOLEAN
      abuses IS A BOOLEAN
      form IS A `Form of conduct`
      dishonest IS A BOOLEAN
      aim IS AN `Aim`
GIVETH AN `Abuse of position case`
`a section 4 case of` occupies abuses form dishonest aim MEANS `Abuse of position case` WITH
    `occupies a position in which he is expected to safeguard, or not to act against, the financial interests of another person` IS occupies
    `abuses that position` IS abuses
    `the conduct that abuses it was` IS form
    `acts dishonestly in abusing it` IS dishonest
    `what the person intends by means of the abuse` IS aim

-- The base case: by an act.
#ASSERT `section 4(1): a person is in breach of section 4` (`a section 4 case of` TRUE TRUE `an act` TRUE `an aim to gain money`)
-- s 4(2): by an omission rather than an act.
#ASSERT `section 4(1): a person is in breach of section 4` (`a section 4 case of` TRUE TRUE `an omission` TRUE `an aim to gain money`)
-- s 4(1)(a): not in such a position.
#ASSERT NOT `section 4(1): a person is in breach of section 4` (`a section 4 case of` FALSE TRUE `an act` TRUE `an aim to gain money`)
-- s 4(1)(b): did not abuse it.
#ASSERT NOT `section 4(1): a person is in breach of section 4` (`a section 4 case of` TRUE FALSE `an act` TRUE `an aim to gain money`)
-- s 4(1)(b): abused it, but not dishonestly.
#ASSERT NOT `section 4(1): a person is in breach of section 4` (`a section 4 case of` TRUE TRUE `an act` FALSE `an aim to gain money`)
-- s 4(1)(c): no aim.
#ASSERT NOT `section 4(1): a person is in breach of section 4` (`a section 4 case of` TRUE TRUE `an act` TRUE `no aim at all`)
-- s 4(1)(c)(ii): aim to expose another to a risk of loss.
#ASSERT `section 4(1): a person is in breach of section 4` (`a section 4 case of` TRUE TRUE `an omission` TRUE `an aim to risk loss of money`)
#ASSERT `section 4(2): conduct that is an act or an omission may be an abuse` `an omission`
#ASSERT `section 4(2): conduct that is an act or an omission may be an abuse` `an act`

§§ `Section 1: fraud`

`the section 2 case in breach` MEANS `a section 2 case of` `a false statement of fact made to a person` TRUE `an aim to gain money`
`the section 2 case not in breach` MEANS `a section 2 case of` `a false statement of fact made to a person` FALSE `an aim to gain money`
`the section 3 case in breach` MEANS `a section 3 case of` TRUE TRUE TRUE `an aim to gain money`
`the section 3 case not in breach` MEANS `a section 3 case of` FALSE TRUE TRUE `an aim to gain money`
`the section 4 case in breach` MEANS `a section 4 case of` TRUE TRUE `an act` TRUE `an aim to gain money`
`the section 4 case not in breach` MEANS `a section 4 case of` FALSE TRUE `an act` TRUE `an aim to gain money`

-- s 1(1), (2): guilty of fraud if in breach of any of the three sections.
#ASSERT `section 1(1) and (2): a person is guilty of fraud` `the section 2 case in breach` `the section 3 case not in breach` `the section 4 case not in breach`
#ASSERT `section 1(1) and (2): a person is guilty of fraud` `the section 2 case not in breach` `the section 3 case in breach` `the section 4 case not in breach`
#ASSERT `section 1(1) and (2): a person is guilty of fraud` `the section 2 case not in breach` `the section 3 case not in breach` `the section 4 case in breach`
#ASSERT `section 1(1) and (2): a person is guilty of fraud` `the section 2 case in breach` `the section 3 case in breach` `the section 4 case in breach`
-- In breach of none of them: not guilty of fraud.
#ASSERT NOT `section 1(1) and (2): a person is guilty of fraud` `the section 2 case not in breach` `the section 3 case not in breach` `the section 4 case not in breach`
